  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'imagine being so disgusting there have to be laws to try to stop normal people from hating you' because the text uses second-person address ('you') to directly engage the viewer, inviting them to imagine themselves in the position of the 'disgusting' entity. This creates a direct semiotic projection where the user is metaphorically placed in the role of the subject of the text's hypothetical scenario.",
